quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  7,88,"The influential leaders of his people, who were arrogant, said: ‘We shall surely expel you, O Shu‘ayb, and those who believe along with you from our town, or else you shall revert to our religion.’ He said: ‘Even if we are unwilling (to join you)?"
  7,89,"Indeed, we would be fabricating a lie against Allah if we reverted to your religion after Allah had delivered us from it. It is inappropriate for us to return to it unless Allah, our Lord, should wish so. Our Lord comprehends all things in (His) knowledge. In Allah, we have put our trust.’ ‘Our Lord! Decide truthfully between us and our people, for You are the best judge.’"
  7,90,"The influential leaders of his people, who disbelieved, said (to the weak ones): ‘If you follow Shu‘ayb, you shall surely be losers.’"
  7,91,"Then the (overwhelming) earthquake overtook them, and by the following morning, they were lying dead in their homes."
  7,92,Those who denied Shu‘ayb were (eliminated) as if they had never lived there. Those who denied Shu‘ayb were themselves the losers.
  7,93,So he turned away from them and said: ‘O my people! I indeed conveyed to you the messages of my Lord and gave you sincere advice.’ Then how should I grieve for a disbelieving people?’
  7,94,"And whenever We sent a prophet to any town, We afflicted its (disbelieving, arrogant) people with suffering and adversity so that they might humble themselves."
  7,95,"Then We replaced (their) adversity with prosperity until they flourished (in multiple numbers) and said: ‘Hardship and affluence (also) befell our forefathers.’ Then, We overtook them suddenly while they were unaware."
